{"name":"Upstate","hex":"#cac7b8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"upstate","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The northern section of a state.","The inland section of a state, particularly of South Carolina."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the northern section of a state."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upstate"}],"entries":[{"title":"Maine","blocks":[{"text":"Maine is a state in the New England region of the United States, and the northeasternmost state in the contiguous United States. It borders New Hampshire to the west, the Gulf of Maine to the southeast, and the Canadian provinces of New Brunswick and Quebec to the northeast and northwest, and shares a maritime border with Nova Scotia. It is the only state to border only one other state. Maine is the largest state in New England by total area, almost as large as the combined area of the remaining five states. Of the 50 U.S. states, it is the 12th-smallest by area, the 9th-least populous, the 13th-least densely populated, and the most rural. As of 2024, Maine's population stood at a Census-estimated 1,400,000, the state's highest-ever population estimate. Maine's capital is Augusta, while its most populous city is Portland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Flag_of_the_State_of_Maine.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_State_of_Maine.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maine"},{"title":"Upstate California","blocks":[{"text":"Upstate California is the name of a marketing campaign which seeks to promote business in the northernmost 20 counties of California. Roughly the upper half of Northern California, the \"upstate\" designation encompasses primarily rural areas which contain 4.5% of California's population. Outside of public relations, this area is often referred to as far Northern California."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Map_of_Northern_and_Upstate_California.png/330px-Map_of_Northern_and_Upstate_California.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Upstate_California"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/2003_ME_Proof.png/500px-2003_ME_Proof.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/2003_ME_Proof.png/500px-2003_ME_Proof.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2003_ME_Proof.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/The_Maine_State_Capitol_building_in_Augusta.jpg/500px-The_Maine_State_Capitol_building_in_Augusta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/The_Maine_State_Capitol_building_in_Augusta.jpg/1280px-The_Maine_State_Capitol_building_in_Augusta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/The_Maine_State_Capitol_building_in_Augusta.jpg/500px-The_Maine_State_Capitol_building_in_Augusta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Maine State House, designed by Charles Bulfinch, built 1829–1832","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Maine_State_Capitol_building_in_Augusta.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Brooklyn_Museum_-_Misty_Morning%2C_Coast_of_Maine_-_Arthur_Parton_-_overall.jpg/500px-Brooklyn_Museum_-_Misty_Morning%2C_Coast_of_Maine_-_Arthur_Parton_-_overall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Brooklyn_Museum_-_Misty_Morning%2C_Coast_of_Maine_-_Arthur_Parton_-_overall